	(text "Supply node of the ladder.\nC62 and the damped branch\nR87, C63 take the current\nof the supply leads when the\nover-current trip opens the\noutput in ampere mode.\nSimulated: SUPPLY stays 0.5 V\nor more below +12V_A then.\nThe bleed resistor of this\nnode is on the Shunt Ladder\nsheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245.11 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "75c29d26-9e28-5e4f-9b64-88c4e32d897d")
	)
	(text "VIN: 0.8 V to 5.0 V in use. With the ampere pair\nopen the terminal withstands -20 V to +20 V and\ntakes less than 1 mA (simulated). With the pair\nclosed the supply has to stay in its range.\nD14 takes hot-plug rings and the kick of the\nsupply leads; it conducts from 22.2 V (datasheet):\nnever a 24 V supply. F1 does not protect D14.\nDetector: VIN_OV goes high at 5.46 V and low\nagain at 5.35 V (calculated; 2.5 V at the tap\nof R73 and R74), 5.41 V to 5.51 V and 5.30 V\nto 5.40 V with the tolerances. Not latched.\nD15 keeps the input within a diode drop of both\nrails; R73 limits its current to 0.17 mA at\n20 V (calculated)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.65 166.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1421894-b5a2-55b9-b310-fb0a3cab3843")
	)
	(text "Mode pairs: Q4, Q8 pass the regulator output (source mode), Q5, Q9 pass VIN\n(ampere mode). Both are open at reset. The gate networks are alike; for the ampere pair:\nClosing: R80 charges the gate against C61, R82: (100 k + 6.8 k) x 100 nF = 10.7 ms,\nafter a first step of 0.76 V, below the threshold (calculated). The pair closes as a\nsource follower: SUPPLY rises with about 0.9 V/ms, full gate drive in 40 ms (simulated).\nOpening: D17 (pin 1 to 3) and R79 discharge the gate at once: one pair is open\nbefore the other conducts. D17 (pin 3 to 2) bounds the gate at +12V_A plus two drops.\nQ7 joins gate and common source while that node is below ground: an open pair stays\nopen with a reversed supply. D19 (pins 2 and 3 joined) holds the base one diode drop\nbelow the emitter otherwise. R84 returns the gate to the common source and keeps 95.7 %\nof the drive (calculated); no resistor goes from a gate to ground. TP32 and TP31 sit\non 100 k nodes: a x10 probe lowers the gate by about 1 % (calculated).\nTP28, TP29: probe grounds at the two mode pairs.\n\nRequests: R70 and R71 hold GATE_SRC and GATE_AMP low while the controller pins float.\nQ2 holds the ampere request low at U20 while source mode is requested, Q3 while\nVIN_OV is high: the two pairs are never closed together, whatever the controller asks.\nR75 and R72 limit the current into U20 while +12V_A is absent (2.7 mA, calculated).\nFirmware leaves 5 ms between lowering one request and raising either; a pair counts as\nclosed 40 ms after its request, and the output switch closes after the mode pair."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 16.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c509a1d4-5832-5f63-adf4-dc91b02625c7")
	)
